## 📌 Project Overview

The **RPCE** (*Entropic Control Pasta Reactor*) is an open-hardware and firmware framework designed to eliminate the risks of wild pyrolysis and fires during starch microwave cooking in closed environments.

Instead of responding with oversimplified warnings or frustrating error messages, the RPCE utilizes an infrared feedback loop and a piezoelectric injector to maintain entropy variation ($\Delta S$) strictly below the critical carbonization threshold.

